  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;be two vectors, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>. Then the projection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
